The timeline now sits in the header row, between the breadcrumbs and the quick links, and the separate timeline row is gone. At 1440px the header is one 72px row on `/` and `/tags`. `scripts/check.sh` fails only in e2e. I closed the bead.

**What changed**
- `PublicHeader.ts` renders `#timeline-mount` inside the header and fills the `timeline` slot itself. `HomePage`, `TagPage`, `tags-graph` and `tags-map` pass their timeline settings to the header instead of rendering their own mount.
- `atlasLayerLayout.ts` and `atlas.css` no longer add a timeline height under the header. `gridFit.ts` no longer measures the timeline mount separately, since it is inside the header.
- CSS source changes are in `header.css`, `timeline.css` and `atlas.css`, and `build-css.sh` was run.
- The atlas header e2e test now asserts the timeline sits inside the header and the map starts below the header.

**Checks**
- **1440px:** the timeline fills the gap and the header height is one row.
- **390px:** the header wraps, with the timeline on its own row, until US-009 adds the responsive collapse. This is the one acceptance criterion this task only partly meets.
- **`/tags` at 1440px:** the timeline is narrow because the tag filter box competes for the same space. I did not fix this.
- **e2e failures:** the atlas "free drag" gesture test and the Trusted Types tags-map marker-click test fail. Both failed the same way on the stashed baseline, so they are not caused by this change.
- **Content clipped:** the old histogram timeline is now clipped to header height. US-002 replaces its content.

I added the learnings to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

